Z||000000||BENGAL4||11-26-1999||11:21 AM||||I have an interesting dillima and I would like my friends on the forum to give their opinion.<P>2 years ago, I was approached by a Fiero owner wanting to sell a TPI 350V8 with a manual trans, set up and on the cradle, ready to install. I told him that I wasn't interested but he gave me his business card and I put it in the sunvisor pocket and forgot about it.<P>Since then, I have purchased an 86GT parts car with the intention of rebuilding the 2.8L and adding a turbo. Well I was looking for something in the sunvisor pocket and I find this business card from 2 years ago. Out of curiosity, I call the number and the guy still has the V8 set up for sale. The price is reasonable so now I have a decision to make. <P>So give me your opinions fellow forum members and lets see what I decide.  <P>P.S.<P>I will be doing all of the work myself and I figure that the price of the rebuild vs the V8 will be +/- $1,000.00. <BR>  <p>[This message has been edited by BENGAL4 (edited 11-26-1999).]||||reg||5
Z||000001||batboy||11-26-1999||12:47 PM||||There are pros and cons for every swap and the V8 conversion is not without headaches, but considering this is a complete V8 engine setup and tranny on a Fiero cradle, I'd be hard pressed not to buy it if, I were you. But hey, that's just me.||||reg||1
Z||000002||chris6878||11-27-1999||12:59 AM||||i say go for the v8...     im planning on the same for my 85 gt. You can get lots of horsepower out of these engines without adding turbo and such....    and they can definately handle the power too.. <P>just my two cents worth...<BR>chris||||reg||10
